  ('1122664334787997398', 'Young Mr. Lincoln', 1939, 'Drama, History', 'John Ford, Bert Glennon', 'Lamar Trotti', 'Henry Fonda, Alice Brady, Marjorie Weaver, Arleen Whelan, Eddie Collins, Pauline Moore, Richard Cromwell, Donald Meek', 'NR', 'In this dramatized account of his early law career in Illinois, Abraham Lincoln is born into a modest log cabin, where he is encouraged by his first love, Ann Rutledge, to pursue law. Following her tragic death, Lincoln establishes a law practice in Springfield, where he meets a young Mary Todd. Lincoln''s law skills are put to the test when he takes on the difficult task of defending two brothers who have been accused of murder.', 'In this dramatized account of his early law career in Illinois, Abraham Lincoln is born into a modest log cabin, where he is encouraged by his first love, Ann Rutledge, to pursue law. Following her tragic death, Lincoln establishes a law practice in Springfield, where he meets a young Mary Todd. Lincoln''s law skills are put to the test when he takes on the difficult task of defending two brothers who have been accused of murder.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/gVHbi2AZfWsZB10FJcwaFV59kIo.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:43838'),
